{% extends '@rental/management/_booking_frame.html.twig' %}
{#
  The dashboard of one booking's file (§6.4, §6.12, §6.15, §6.16): the first
  of its four pages (Booking\BookingPage), and the one a link to the booking
  lands on.

  **Read top to bottom, in three movements.** Where the booking stands and
  what to do about it (the journey, one component: `_journey.html.twig`),
  what the booking is, and then what it has gathered that is not money,
  papers or mail — those have a page each, one chip away.

  The journey and the checklist are ONE derivation (Booking\BookingJourney
  stages what Booking\BookingMilestones computed), so the heading, the five
  stretches and the fifteen lines can never tell different stories. A line
  still renders greyed when it belongs to something this installation does
  not do at all (no security deposit configured, no meter on the asset): an
  unreachable box reads as outstanding work. A step whose work is done on
  another page links there with the box's anchor (`BookingBox::href()`),
  and collapse-anchor.js opens that box on arrival.

  **A box's fold is deliberately OUTSIDE its wrapper.** The `.collapse` and
  the button that toggles it belong to the card; only the body and the
  figure are swapped by the page's refresh. Adding a comment therefore
  leaves the box open at the line you were reading, where re-rendering the
  card around it would have folded the box under your hands. The journey's
  own stretches are the exception and it is the right one: an action that
  moves the booking on moves which stretch is current, and the fresh render
  opening the new one is the answer, not a lost place.
#}
{% block booking_content %}
        {# ── 1. Où en est cette réservation ────────────────────────── #}
        {% include '@rental/management/_journey.html.twig' %}

        {# ── 2. Les détails de la réservation ──────────────────────── #}
        {#
          Who, what, when, how much — and no status badge: the journey above
          already answers « où en est cette réservation ? », and two answers
          to one question on one page is the defect this page exists to fix.
        #}
        <div data-booking-panel="renter">
        <div class="card mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="h5 mb-3">Les détails de la réservation</h2>
                <dl class="row mb-0">
                    <dt class="col-sm-4">Locataire</dt>
                    <dd class="col-sm-8">{{ booking.renterName }}</dd>
                    <dt class="col-sm-4">Email</dt>
                    <dd class="col-sm-8"><a href="mailto:{{ booking.renterEmail }}">{{ booking.renterEmail }}</a></dd>
                    {% if booking.renterPhone %}
                        <dt class="col-sm-4">Téléphone</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-8"><a href="tel:{{ booking.renterPhone|replace({' ': ''}) }}">{{ booking.renterPhone }}</a></dd>
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if booking.renterOrganisation %}
                        <dt class="col-sm-4">Organisation</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-8">{{ booking.renterOrganisation }}</dd>
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if booking.purpose %}
                        <dt class="col-sm-4">Objet</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-8">{{ booking.purpose }}</dd>
                    {% endif %}
                    <dt class="col-sm-4">Dates</dt>
                    <dd class="col-sm-8">
                        du {{ booking.arrivalDate|date_fr }} au {{ booking.departureDate|date_fr }}
                    </dd>
                    {% if booking.estimatedPersons %}
                        <dt class="col-sm-4">Participants annoncés</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-8">{{ booking.estimatedPersons }}</dd>
                    {% endif %}
                    <dt class="col-sm-4">Total</dt>
                    <dd class="col-sm-8">
                        {{ quote.totalCents|money_cents }}
                        {% if payment.available and payment.enabled %}
                            <span class="text-body-secondary small d-block">
                                {{ payment.received_cents|money_cents }} reçus
                                {%- if payment.remaining_cents > 0 %}, {{ payment.remaining_cents|money_cents }} dus{% endif %}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </dd>
                    {% if booking.renterComment %}
                        <dt class="col-sm-4">Message</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-8">{{ booking.renterComment|nl2br }}</dd>
                    {% endif %}
                </dl>

                {# The tracking link is shown nowhere: holding it IS the
                   authorisation (§8.52). So it is never retrieved — it is
                   replaced, and the new one goes to the renter by email. #}
                <form method="post" action="/mes-locations/lien-suivi" class="mt-3"
                      data-confirm="Régénérer le lien ? L'ancien cessera de fonctionner et le locataire devra recevoir le nouveau.">
                    {{ csrf_field()|raw }}
                    <input type="hidden" name="asset_id" value="{{ asset.id }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="booking_id" value="{{ booking.id }}">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">
                        Régénérer le lien de suivi
                    </button>
                    <div class="form-text">
                        À faire si le locataire a perdu son lien, ou l'a transmis à quelqu'un
                        qui ne devait pas le recevoir. Le nouveau lien lui est envoyé par email.
                    </div>
                </form>
            </div>
        </div>
        </div>

        {# ── 3. Le dossier ─────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        {#
          What the booking gathered that is neither money, papers nor mail:
          the renter's requests, the stay, the internal comments and the
          history. Folded, each line carrying its figure.
        #}
        <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Le dossier</h2>
        <p class="text-body-secondary small">
            Chaque boîte s'ouvre d'un clic ; le chiffre à côté de son nom dit ce qu'elle contient.
        </p>

        {% include '@rental/management/_box_changes.html.twig' %}

        {#
          The stay is a page of its own, so its line is a link rather than a
          fold — the only one in the list, and it says so by carrying an
          arrow instead of a chevron.
        #}
        <div class="card mb-3" id="{{ boxes.stay.anchor }}">
            <a class="card-body d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2 text-decoration-none"
               href="{{ boxes.stay.href(booking_url) }}">
                <span>
                    <span class="h6 mb-0">{{ boxes.stay.label }}</span>
                    <span class="text-body-secondary small d-block">
                        Relevés de compteurs, état des lieux, incidents et décompte final.
                    </span>
                </span>
                <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right text-body-tertiary" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </a>
        </div>

        {% include '@rental/management/_box_comments.html.twig' %}
        {% include '@rental/management/_box_history.html.twig' %}
{% endblock %}

{% block booking_scripts %}{% endblock %}
